From: Luca Weiss <luca.weiss@fairphone.com>
Subject: [FROMLIST v1] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7225-fairphone-fp4: Disable PMK8350 PON

Two PMICs on this phone have a PON (power-on / reboot-reason) block, the
PM6350 and the PMK8350. Only one should be enabled at a time. With both
enabled the reboot-mode wiring breaks, so `reboot bootloader` and
`reboot recovery` no longer reach the bootloader (they boot straight back
into the OS). Keep the PM6350 PON, which carries the mode-bootloader /
mode-recovery magics (pm6350.dtsi), and disable the PMK8350 PON.

Upstream commit 844d77d0bf8d ("arm64: dts: qcom: sm7225-fairphone-fp4:
Disable PMK8350 PON"), Fixes: 582e7c1026fa ("arm64: dts: qcom:
sm7225-fairphone-fp4: Add pmk8350 PMIC"). Not yet in the pinned base tag
(v7.2.0-sm6350 = 16337c9dd348), so carried here as a patch until the pin
advances.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7225-fairphone-fp4.dts | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7225-fairphone-fp4.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7225-fairphone-fp4.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7225-fairphone-fp4.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7225-fairphone-fp4.dts
@@ -1746,3 +1746,15 @@ &wifi {

 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+/*
+ * Two PMICs on this phone have a PON block, the PM6350 and PMK8350. Only one
+ * should be enabled at a time, so disable PMK8350 PON and keep PM6350 PON
+ * (which carries the reboot-mode magics). Having both breaks reboot-mode, so
+ * `reboot bootloader` / `reboot recovery` no longer reach the bootloader.
+ * Upstream: Luca Weiss, "arm64: dts: qcom: sm7225-fairphone-fp4: Disable
+ * PMK8350 PON" (FROMLIST, Fixes: 582e7c1026fa).
+ */
+&pmk8350_pon {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
